+### QR Print helper (local follow-up, 2026-10-22)
+
+The helper on PR #590 builds a print sheet from serialized items and item families, keeps printed text editable without changing scan identity, and downloads one CSV per Brother template. Numbered family labels derive the full `{familyQr}-{unitNumber}` identity. Downloading is separate from deliberately confirming that physical labels were printed and applied (D-022).
+
+Local audit fixes block invalid/unknown unit picks and failed unit reads from silently producing partial files, track download freshness by file contents, preserve cumulative downloaded unit batches, repair all six `.lbx` merge bindings, and constrain/center text separately from the QR. All QR templates use the user-requested Medium Small cells and the existing Gotham typography. Payloads that would grow beyond version 1 / M require a wider-tape layout instead of changing the stored scan identity.
+
+The approved 21 px Gotham XNarrow Bold layout is now the local default. The refined sheet displays 76 px previews (up from 44 px), centered in preview trays, with a 152 px inspection dialog. Product names replace native template filenames in normal controls. The gear picker, custom-label forms and USB status area share clearer hierarchy; the two-column layout starts at `xl` to preserve picker space beside the app sidebar. A shared exact-outline renderer produces the same monochrome bitmap for preview and direct USB printing. Medium Small QR cores remain 63 dots at 180 dpi; the body/lens sample is centered on a 194×76-dot printable image. Other label kinds fit text independently, and unsupported glyphs or oversized text block the complete USB batch before printer writes.
+
+Direct USB controls support the PT-D610BT (`04f9:20e1`) in desktop Chrome/Edge, with 12 mm laminated white-on-black media checks. The label route alone enables USB in its Permissions Policy (plus the development-only fixture). A Web Lock covers connection, printing and cleanup; immutable batches are capped at 500 labels, completion is counted per label, and a durable local receipt survives reloads. Stop finishes the current label. Unknown outcomes pause reconnect and printing until physical review; no batch automatically resumes or retries. Printer completion only makes those exact units eligible for the existing deliberate printed/applied confirmation under D-022.
+
+CSV export remains secondary and uses the native templates' separate layout. P-touch's one-record merge limitation is explicit; USB is the single-label path. Local browser proof covers partial completion, unknown output, delayed chooser races, reload recovery, exact unit marking, safe stop, and tablet/phone widths. An initial integrated attempt stopped before raster setup because it reset an already-selected USB alternate. The corrected setup preserves that active interface. The helper then received a no-error completion for one FB FX3 1 label, and the user confirmed centered/unclipped output, larger Gotham, and the correct production scan. Authenticated feature-route proof remains unavailable because PR #590 has no managed preview environment. The 12 mm tape cannot provide the full nominal four-module quiet zone; all-six-template physical acceptance is separate. See [the audit ledger](../tasks/qr-print-audit-plan-2026-10-22.md).
+
 ### Inventory Hygiene
 1. Staff/admin opens the "Keep data clean" lane on `/operations` (the old `/items/hygiene` route redirects there).
 2. The lane shows cleanup checks that improve picker, search, checkout, kit, and scan quality.
